    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d131">

                <pb facs="0166" n="92" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v01/pg92"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 868.00/116</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Greece</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Droppers</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Athens</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-06-12T11:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">June 12, 1917, 11 a.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 12 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>352. King has abdicated. Ultimatum gives him 48 hours to go. His second son,
                        Alexander, to be proclaimed King. Crown
                    Prince who was abler but entertained Germanophile opinions has renounced rights
                    of succession to the throne. Order prevailed during night but confidence not yet
                    restored. Ex-Monarch going to England, he would have preferred Switzerland.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Droppers</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
